[{:adr/consequences "{:symmetry \"Ghost Hacker's three living surfaces now each have the standalone\\n             repo shape ADR-2607011816 established as this franchise's norm:\\n             Ren's line (orgs/com-junkawasaki/ghosthacker), SHIRO & PICO's\\n             narrative content (orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico),\\n             and now the game project (orgs/gftdcojp/isekai-network)\", :decoupled_from_engine_churn \"isekai-network's lifecycle (design iteration,\\n                                 future concept prototypes) no longer shares a\\n                                 repo, issue tracker, or commit history with\\n                                 kami-engine's in-progress clj-wgsl Rust-removal\\n                                 migration (ADR-2607010930)\", :engine_dependency_unchanged \"isekai-network still depends on kami-engine as an\\n                                 external engine (a west sibling project) for\\n                                 anything beyond `clojure -M author.clj` --\\n                                 concept 1's WASM compile remains blocked on that\\n                                 migration landing a working kamiclj-equivalent\\n                                 entry point, tracked as it was in PR #91, now\\n                                 tracked from isekai-network's own README instead\", :zero_kami_engine_footprint \"kami-engine's git history has no isekai-network\\n                                commits at all (PR closed unmerged, not merged\\n                                then reverted) -- clean separation\"}", :adr/authoritative_for ["Ghost Hacker: Shiro & Pico (game project codename isekai-network) lives at\n    orgs/gftdcojp/isekai-network, not nested under kotoba-lang/kami-engine's\n    kami-clj-play/games/" "kotoba-lang/kami-engine PR #91 (the initial kami-clj-play/games/isekai-network/\n    placement) was closed unmerged, superseded by this split -- kami-engine has\n    zero net footprint from this game project" "the 5-concept EDN game bible (design/00-game-bible.edn + 01..05) and the\n    concept-1 prototype (author.clj/logic.clj, clojure -M author.clj verified\n    working end-to-end) moved verbatim into the new repo's design/ and\n    games/01-netsurvivors/ -- no content changes, only relocation" "the WASM-compile blocker found while authoring the kami-engine PR (kami-engine-clj\n    deleted upstream in kotoba-lang/kotoba PR #259, part of the in-progress\n    clj-wgsl migration, ADR-2607010930) is orthogonal to this repo-placement\n    decision and remains open regardless of where the game code lives"], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "isekai-network-split", :adr/related ["CLAUDE.md" "90-docs/adr/2607011816-ghosthacker-shiropico-standalone-repo.md" "90-docs/adr/2607010930-clj-wgsl-migration.md" "manifest/repos.edn" "orgs/kotoba-lang/kami-engine PR #91 (closed, superseded)" "orgs/gftdcojp/isekai-network"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607023200-isekai-network-standalone-repo", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-02", :adr/decision "{:new_repo {:path \"orgs/gftdcojp/isekai-network\", :remote \"gftdcojp\", :visibility :private, :org_default_visibility_source \"repos.edn :orgs :visibility (gftdcojp = private, per CLAUDE.md standing policy, ADR-2607021330)\", :method \"plain copy of the 12 git-tracked files from kami-engine's\\n                      kami-clj-play/games/isekai-network/ -> new repo, restructured\\n                      as design/*.edn (unchanged) + games/01-netsurvivors/* (unchanged\\n                      content, author.clj re-verified with `clojure -M author.clj`\\n                      from the new location), git init, one commit, gh repo create\\n                      --source=. --push (same pattern as ADR-2607011816's\\n                      ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico split)\"}, :source_pr_change {:repo \"orgs/kotoba-lang/kami-engine\", :action \"PR #91 closed unmerged (not merged-then-reverted) -- superseded by orgs/gftdcojp/isekai-network\", :unaffected \"kami-clj-play/games/{survivors,waves} and all other kami-engine content -- PR #91 only ever touched the new isekai-network/ subtree\"}, :manifest_registration {:repos_edn \"add \\\"orgs/gftdcojp/isekai-network\\\" to :extra-projects via GitHub\\n               Contents API single-entry commit (blob-sha-matched PUT against\\n               origin/main tip), not a local edit -- same method ADR-2607011816\\n               used, for the same reason: this superproject checkout has\\n               concurrent-fleet pin drift and shallow-clone '(forced update)'\\n               noise that make a local edit + full regen risky\", :west_yml \"add one project entry (name/remote/revision/path/groups),\\n              alphabetically placed, mirroring the ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico\\n              entry's shape, via the same API method\", :why_api_not_local \"identical rationale to ADR-2607011816: avoids a stale-base\\n                        3-way merge against a moving main tip, and avoids bundling\\n                        unrelated drifted child-repo pins into a one-line\\n                        registration commit (the 'pin regression trap' repos.edn's\\n                        :manifest-workflow warns about)\", :verify \"pin == orgs/gftdcojp/isekai-network@main HEAD confirmed before commit;\\n            nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs --check run after to confirm the\\n            hand-placed entries match canonical generator output\"}}", :db/id -1, :adr/problem "{:source \"user request 2026-07-02: '個別のゲームは isekai-network repo にまとめてね' (consolidate the individual games into the isekai-network repo), sent while kotoba-lang/kami-engine PR #91 was open for review\", :investigated [\"PR #91 held the full deliverable so far: design/00-game-bible.edn (title\\n    'Ghost Hacker: Shiro & Pico', cast, bestiary, shared controls/tone/rating)\\n    + design/01..05.edn (one per concept variant) + a real concept-1 prototype\\n    (author.clj/logic.clj, a faithful rename+recolour of\\n    kami-clj-play/games/survivors onto the shiro-pico/ghost cast) -- review\\n    found it clean (CI green, mergeable) with no correctness issues\" \"ADR-2607011816 already resolved the identical structural question for\\n    this franchise's narrative content: ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico was\\n    split out of ai-gftd-mangaka specifically to decouple an independently-\\n    lifecycled IP from an unrelated engine/infra repo's churn, and to match\\n    the standalone-repo symmetry Ren's Ghost Hacker line already has\\n    (orgs/com-junkawasaki/ghosthacker). The same reasoning transfers directly\\n    to the game project: kami-engine is mid an active internal migration\\n    (ADR-2607010930, clj-wgsl, which had already deleted the kami-engine-clj\\n    Rust crate PR #91's own README depended on) -- coupling a product-shaped\\n    game's lifecycle to that churn is the same mistake ADR-2607011816 already\\n    named and rejected once for this franchise\" \"west.yml's own kami-app-{game} convention (ARCHITECTURE.md) already\\n    treats new games as separate per-game crates/repos, not nested paths --\\n    a standalone isekai-network repo is consistent with that convention too,\\n    not just with the shiropico content-split precedent\"], :risk \"PR #91 was clean and mergeable; closing it unmerged rather than\\n         merging-then-deleting avoids ever landing content in kami-engine's\\n         history that would need a follow-up removal commit\"}", :adr/alternatives "[{:option \"merge PR #91 as-is, keep the game nested in kami-engine's kami-clj-play/games/isekai-network/\", :rejected_because \"explicit user direction to consolidate into a dedicated repo; also repeats the exact coupling-to-unrelated-engine-churn mistake ADR-2607011816 already identified and rejected for this franchise's narrative content\"} {:option \"name the new repo ai-gftd-isekai-network, matching gftdcojp's ai-gftd-* naming convention (ai-gftd-mangaka, ai-gftd-animeka, ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico)\", :rejected_because \"user explicitly requested the literal name 'isekai-network repo' -- honoring the exact requested name over imposing an unrequested naming convention\"} {:option \"merge PR #91 into kami-engine first, then separately create isekai-network and delete the kami-engine copy in a follow-up commit\", :rejected_because \"would leave a needless detour through kami-engine's git history; closing the clean, unmerged PR directly is simpler and leaves zero trace, matching how ADR-2607012000's abandoned michibiki-repo detour was handled (deleted before ever landing, no trace in history)\"}]", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607023200: isekai-network (Ghost Hacker: Shiro & Pico game) as a standalone repo, not nested in kami-engine"}]